The Pentagon [hardened its ultimatum to Anthropic](https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-02-26/pentagon-hardens-its-ultimatum-to-anthropic-in-feud-over-ai-use) on Thursday, making public a Friday 5:01 PM deadline for the company to grant unrestricted military access to Claude or face designation as a ["supply chain risk"](https://abcnews.com/Politics/pentagon-anthropic-ultimatum-ai-technology-sources/story?id=130498030) — a label normally reserved for foreign adversaries like Huawei. Defense Secretary Hegseth's office has already [called Boeing and Lockheed Martin](https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/technology/tech-news/how-the-pentagons-friday-deadline-may-have-come-hours-early-for-anthropic/articleshow/128819123.cms) to audit their exposure to Claude, preparation for severance before the deadline even arrives. The threat is surgical: a supply chain designation would force every defense contractor to certify they don't use Claude in military-adjacent work, making the most capable AI model [radioactive across the entire industrial base](https://techstartups.com/2026/02/25/pentagon-gives-anthropic-friday-deadline-to-lift-claude-military-limits-or-face-defense-production-act/). The day before the ultimatum, the Pentagon signed xAI to a deal deploying [Grok on classified networks](https://www.teslarati.com/xais-grok-approved-for-pentagon-classified-systems-report/) for intelligence analysis, weapons development, and battlefield operations — xAI agreed to the "all lawful purposes" standard [without reservation](https://opentools.ai/news/elon-musks-xai-lands-pentagon-pact-to-deploy-grok-ai-in-classified-ops). The replacement was lined up before the threat was delivered.

**Nvidia printed a record quarter and the market punished it anyway.** Q4 revenue hit [$68.1 billion](http://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-fourth-quarter-and-fiscal-2026), up 73% year-over-year, with Data Center at [$62.3 billion](https://www.techpowerup.com/346767/nvidia-reports-record-usd-68-1b-q4-revenue-usd-215-9b-for-fiscal-2026) and networking revenue tripling to $11 billion. Full-year revenue crossed [$215.9 billion](https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/25/nvidia-nvda-q4-2026-earnings-call-transcript/). Jensen Huang guided Q1 to $78 billion, [smashing consensus](https://fortune.com/2026/02/25/nvidia-nvda-earnings-q4-results-jensen-huang/) of $72.6 billion, and declared "the agentic AI inflection point has arrived." The stock [dropped 5.5%](https://blockonomi.com/nvidia-stock-slides-5-after-strong-q4-earnings-beat/), wiping $259 billion in market cap in a single session. Michael Burry published a [Substack warning](https://www.businessinsider.com/big-short-michael-burry-nvidia-risk-earnings-stock-ai-bubble-2026-2) that Nvidia's purchase obligations surged from $16 billion to $95 billion in twelve months — noncancelable orders placed before demand is known — drawing a parallel to [Cisco at the dot-com peak](https://www.cnbc.com/2026/02/26/michael-burry-sees-nvidia-parallel-to-cisco-at-dot-com-bubble-top.html). On the earnings call, Huang acknowledged that [orbital data centers have "poor economics today"](https://www.businessinsider.com/nvidia-jensen-huang-space-data-centers-ai-2026-2) but will improve — a diplomatic way of telling Musk that $68 billion buys a lot of patience on Earth.

**The capability curve is splitting into lanes.** Google launched [Nano Banana 2](https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/build-with-nano-banana-2/) (officially Gemini 3.1 Flash Image), a mixture-of-experts image generator delivering [Pro-quality output at Flash speed](https://arstechnica.com/ai/2026/02/google-releases-nano-banana-2-ai-image-generator-promises-pro-results-with-flash-speed/) with resolutions up to 4K — it becomes the default across Google's ecosystem immediately. Alibaba dropped [Qwen 3.5 Medium](https://venturebeat.com/technology/alibabas-new-open-source-qwen3-5-medium-models-offer-sonnet-4-5-performance), four open-source models under Apache 2.0 that match or beat [GPT-5 mini and Claude Sonnet 4.5](https://the-decoder.com/alibabas-open-qwen-3-5-takes-aim-at-gpt-5-mini-and-claude-sonnet-4-5-at-a-fraction-of-the-cost/) on benchmarks while running on consumer GPUs with 32GB VRAM. Inception Labs unveiled [Mercury 2](https://www.inceptionlabs.ai/blog/introducing-mercury-2), the first reasoning model built on diffusion rather than autoregressive decoding, hitting [1,009 tokens per second](https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260224034496/en/Inception-Launches-Mercury-2-the-Fastest-Reasoning-LLM-5x-Faster-Than-Leading-Speed-Optimized-LLMs-with-Dramatically-Lower-Inference-Cost) on Blackwell GPUs at $0.25 per million input tokens. Musk tweeted that [Grok 4.20 "is getting good at engineering"](https://x.com/elonmusk/status/2027094139096227842). The frontier is no longer a single summit — it's a mountain range.

**The money is arguing with itself.** Citadel Securities [fired back](https://fortune.com/2026/02/26/citadel-demolishes-viral-doomsday-ai-essay-citrini-macro-fundamentals-engels-pause/) at Citrini Research's viral "2028 Global Intelligence Crisis" scenario — the same report that [tanked IBM and software stocks](https://www.wbur.org/hereandnow/2026/02/26/ai-white-collar-jobs-report) earlier this week — arguing the real intelligence crisis is misunderstanding macro fundamentals: software engineer demand is [up 11% year-over-year](https://www.citadelsecurities.com/news-and-insights/2026-global-intelligence-crisis/), AI capex sits at 2% of GDP, and "successive waves of technological change have not rendered labor obsolete." Nvidia is meanwhile [closing a $30 billion equity stake in OpenAI](https://www.reuters.com/business/nvidia-close-finalizing-30-billion-investment-openai-funding-round-ft-reports-2026-02-20/) as part of a $100+ billion round valuing the company at $830 billion — replacing a $100 billion infrastructure commitment with a direct capital bet. The chip supplier is buying the customer is buying the chips.

